SUSPECTED BUG: translation layer end to end, Translate(handleTransfer(...)); domain and infrastructure errors must not
leak. Correct set: fresh *api.Error (400/404/402/500), api.ErrUnavailable, and behind (*api.Error).Unwrap only values
that contain domain.ErrDuplicate (ErrDuplicate behind "transfer %d: %w" x2, plus audit/rollback errors joined to it).
Actual: domain.ErrDuplicate is missing, because execute's set is hidden behind WithTx's "load of escaping variable
err" values (plan S08 is not implemented, see tx_withtx_decl), and handleTransfer's set is cut at
unresolved(fixpoint-limit) (see service_transfer_decl). The entries behind (*api.Error).Unwrap (retry.ErrBusy,
errDryRun, NotFoundError[AccountID], filerepo and audit errors) are not leaks in the tool's model: each belongs to
an errors.Join / double-%w value with a may-match part (an Unresolved value, or a type with a custom Is method),
which errors.Is(err, ErrDuplicate) keeps by the documented rule. Compare api_import_decl, where the same
translation is precise for the part that is visible.
-- args --
api/api.go:@transfer
